#---
# purpose: "macro-emitted defstruct construction and field access reaches the backend: StructDef facts, not the deleted module_struct_fields/struct_schemas source scan, are authoritative for schema lookup"
#---
#
# # macro-emitted defstruct runtime
#
# The old `module_struct_fields`/`struct_schemas` scan was a raw `find_map`
# over top-level `ScopeForm::Struct` source forms, so it never saw a
# `defstruct` a macro expanded into a module body (macro expansions surface as
# `ScopeForm::MacroCall`, not `ScopeForm::Struct`). Backend struct-schema
# lookup now reads the fact-backed `StructDef` store instead, which does see
# macro-emitted structs -- so `Point`, entirely defined through
# `make_struct/1`, must still construct and field-access correctly end to end.
defmacro make_struct(fields) do
  {:defstruct, %{}, [fields]}
end

defmodule Point do
  make_struct([:x, :y])

  fn new(x, y), do: %Point{x: x, y: y}
end

fn main() do
  point = Point.new(3, 4)
  dbg(point.x)
  dbg(point.y)
end
